{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Setting up an Xcode project that uses MapLibre Native for iOS."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/AddMarkerSymbolExample"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/gettingstarted"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Create-a-new-iOS-project","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Create a new iOS project"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a new (SwiftUI) iOS project with Xcode. Go to "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"File > New > Project…"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Add-MapLibre-Native-as-a-dependency","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Add MapLibre Native as a dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MapLibre Native for iOS is available on "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/cocoapods.org","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and on the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/swiftpackageindex.com\/maplibre\/maplibre-gl-native-distribution","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (for use with the Swift Package Manager). However, for this guide we will add the MapLibre Native as a package dependency directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Xcode, right click your project and select “Add Package Dependencies…”:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineCon